# Ad-hoc 3MF fixtures dropped in the repo root while investigating a file (multi-megabyte,
# user-specific). Real fixtures live beside their tests or under /data/demo-library.
/*.3mf
apps/api/data/
apps/api/prisma/data/
# Transient BambuStudio CLI output written to CWD when the slicer (or a manual CLI probe)
# runs in-workspace. Slice output itself goes to SLICER_WORK_DIR (/tmp); this stray file
# lands wherever the CLI was launched from (the slicer workspace or the repo root).
apps/slicer/result.json
/result.json
apps/bridge/data/
apps/bridge/apps/bridge/data/
# Bridge/demo runtime state written relative to CWD when a process is launched from `apps/`
# rather than its own workspace. Holds an installationId + runtimeToken, which are secrets.
# The known cause (a wrong hop count in the demo bootstrap's `repoRoot`) was fixed 2026-09-09 and
# the stray directory deleted, but this stays: the two entries above are the same class of bug from
# other paths, and the cost of being wrong here is committing a live credential.
apps/data/
apps/bridge/release/
apps/bridge/.cache/
apps/server/release/
apps/server/.cache/
# Capacitor's platform trees are generated from the maintained mobile overlays.
# Firebase config and release signing material are injected locally/through CI.
apps/mobile/android/
apps/mobile/ios/
apps/mobile/release.keystore
google-services.json
docs/current-work-status.md
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
.DS_Store
# Deployment-local copies live at the repo root; the nested
/compose.yml
/nginx.conf

# Project-scoped MCP config: holds a per-install localhost token (Integrated
# Browser MCP), so it's developer-local, not shared/committed.
/.mcp.json

# Hand-made backups of the developer-local files above. Ignored by pattern so a
# `cp x x.bak` before a local experiment can't be swept into a commit by
# `git add -A`: the original is already ignored, but the copy was not.
*.bak

# TypeScript incremental build info (per-package, kept out of git/CI)
*.tsbuildinfo

# ESLint results cache (`npm run lint`). Developer-local and machine-specific: it keys results
# on a content hash per file, so sharing it across machines or branches buys nothing and risks
# masking a real finding. CI always runs it cold.
.eslintcache

# Windows client build outputs and local signing material.
apps/desktop/**/bin/
apps/desktop/**/obj/
apps/desktop/artifacts/
apps/desktop/**/*.pfx
